===
# Problem Statement

## The Challenge

Moving from monolithic architecture to distributed microservices while maintaining performance and reliability

::: {background: '#282c34'; padding: '20px'; border-radius: '10px'; border-left: '4px solid #e06c75'}
### Key Issues
- Tight coupling in monolithic system
- Difficulty scaling individual components
- Long deployment cycles
- Single point of failure

:::

===
# Architecture

## System Design

::: {display: 'grid'; grid-template-columns: '1fr 1fr'; gap: '2em'}

### Core Services
- User Service
- Order Service
- Payment Service
- Notification Service

### Tech Stack
- Node.js / Express
- PostgreSQL / Redis
- Docker / Kubernetes
- RabbitMQ / Kafka

:::

===
# Service Communication

## API Gateway Pattern

```javascript [highlight:line-by-line]
class APIGateway {
    constructor(services) {
        this.services = services;
        this.loadBalancer = new LoadBalancer();
    }
    
    async route(request) {
        const service = this.services[request.path];
        const instance = this.loadBalancer.getNext(service);
        return await instance.handle(request);
    }
}
```

===
# Service Implementation

## Microservice Structure

```typescript [highlight:block]
interface Service {
    name: string;
    port: number;
    health: () => Promise<boolean>;
}

class OrderService implements Service {
    name = 'order-service';
    port = 3001;
    
    async health() {
        return this.database.isConnected();
    }
    
    async createOrder(data: OrderData) {
        const order = await this.repository.create(data);
        await this.eventBus.publish('order.created', order);
        return order;
    }
}
```

===
# Event-Driven Architecture

## Asynchronous Communication

::: {display: 'grid'; grid-template-columns: '1fr 1fr'; gap: '2em'}

```javascript [highlight:line-by-line]
// Publisher
eventBus.publish('order.created', {
    orderId: '12345',
    userId: 'user-001',
    amount: 99.99
});
```

```javascript [highlight:line-by-line]
// Subscriber
eventBus.subscribe('order.created', 
    async (event) => {
        await sendConfirmationEmail(event);
        await updateInventory(event);
    }
);
```

:::

